  move q→q2:  q=[]  q2=[3,5]
  q.add(4):   q=[4]  q2=[3,5]
  move q2→q:  q=[4,3,5]  q2=[]

top():      4
pop():      q=[3,5]  q2=[]
size():     2

//////////////////////// QUESTION /////////////////////////////

Stack using Queue
Implement a Stack using Queue data structure. This stack has no fixed capacity and grows dynamically.

Operations:
(i) push(x): Insert element x at the top of the stack
(ii) pop(): Remove element from top (do nothing if empty)
(iii) top(): Return top element, else -1 if empty
(iv) size(): Return number of elements

Query format:
1 x : push(x)
2   : pop()
3   : top()
4   : size()

Examples:
Input: [[1,5],[1,3],[1,4],[3],[2],[4]]
Output: [4,2]
Explanation: push(5), push(3), push(4) → stack: [4,3,5]; top()=4; pop() removes 4; size()=2

Input: [[4],[3],[1,10],[3]]
Output: [0,-1,10]
Explanation: size()=0; top()=-1; push(10); top()=10

Constraints:
1 ≤ queries.size ≤ 100
0 ≤ x ≤ 10^4
